Z||000000||SwissFormula||12-07-2001||07:07 PM||||well, it continues...<P>there is still a lot of bodywork to do. Stripping the old paint was a real PITA,  revealing a lot of filler too:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.darklord.ch/images/pontiac/68gto_ps.jpg">  <P>the engine:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.darklord.ch/images/pontiac/68gto_motor2.jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.darklord.ch/images/pontiac/68gto_motor3.jpg">  <P>I have a set of RAIII heads, have not put them on yet because the engine is running very fine. I KNOW they will be used in near future!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>The car has not been moved for at least 10 years, the engine however was in good shape. Put in fresh oil, new belts, hoses & spark plugs... and it fired up! No intake or exhaust leaks, no dropping oil or whatever, smooth idle, the oil stayed clean after driving ~100km - i was surprised!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>"never touch a running system" came into my mind. I don't think it needs a rebuilt, so the engine was only cleaned & painted.<P>Currently in my dreams: a Fiero with a powerful 400ci Pontiac powerplant, ready to gooooooo!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/burnout.gif">  <P>More GTO-restoration to come afer XMas!<BR>What do you guys think?<P><BR>------------------<BR>Roy<P>88 Formula, T-Top<BR>1 of 20 Fieros in Switzerland<p>[This message has been edited by SwissFormula (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
